        <p>
    Strong Foundation (48-60 points) <br>
    Your responses show distributed leadership thinking across multiple contexts. You focus on building system resilience. You view leadership as developing others’ capabilities rather than keeping control. Unlike Jennifer before her realization, you have likely built systems that pass the “absence test.” 
</p>
<p><strong>Your strengths:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>You develop others’ decision-making skills rather than decide for them</li>
    <li>You build systems that function well without your constant involvement</li>
    <li>You help others become more confident and independent in their roles</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Growth opportunities:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>Share your distributed leadership approach to help others build similar skills</li>
    <li>Look for mentoring opportunities in capability-building leadership and organizational resilience</li>
    <li>Keep studying system health principles for use in complex leadership situations</li>
</ul>
            
